Command Index-
whoami: Returns current user name
id: Returns current user ID as well as your groups
ls -l: See the permissions for a file or directory
chmod: Change permissions on a file or directory.

File Permissions-
r: Read
w: Write
x: Execute
rwx rwx rwx indicates permissions of owner, group, and other in that order
a dash indicates a missing permission, IE: rw- means they cannot execute.

Directory Permissions-
r: List directory contents
w: Create/delete/rename entries
x: Traverse/access

Permissions as numbers-
r: 4
w: 2
x: 1
Permissions for a group/owner are then expressed as a sum, IE: rwx = 7, as 4 + 2 + 1 = 7
And as a set of four for owner, group, and other, IE: 700 = owner has all perms; everyone else has none

